On 12/13/05 3:00 PM, Doug Freyburger wrote:
> Shop keepers appear stupid because the OP is playing on a single-user
> system and the code was designed for multi-user systems.

I suspect that the reason is a simpler one: as long as the savefile 
isn't messed with, the hero's name is the one thing that will never 
change. Gender, alignment, even species can change, but not the name. So 
the shopkeeper recognizes you by name so that you can't, for example, 
poly yourself back into his good graces. It's an in-game issue, rather 
than a between-games issue. On the infrequent occasions it comes up as a 
result of a bones file, it's probably thought of as simply being a part 
of the return-to-the-level phenomenon.

After all, how much *worse* would it be on a multi-user system if you 
happened to choose the same name as someone else who had left a bones 
file with a hostile shopkeeper? "What the heck is he mad at *me* for?"

